# Line endings, settled once, so the scripts in this project still run.
#
# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF by default. Verilog does not care,
# and neither does a simulator. A shell script does: a `.sh` with CRLF run under
# Cygwin or MSYS fails with `$'\r': command not found`, and the first thing it
# fails on is usually `.agent/rtlgraph/run-tb.sh` — the one command that says
# whether the design passes.
#
# RTLGraph wrote this file because the project did not have one. It is yours
# now: edit it, and `Copy Agent Spec to Workspace` will leave it alone.

* text=auto

# Run by a shell, so LF wherever they are checked out.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf
*.mk      text eol=lf
# `#!/usr/bin/env node` on a CRLF line is not a shebang either.
*.mjs     text eol=lf

# Read by tools rather than diffed by people, and large.
*.vcd     -text
